     [38;5;246mlogin(username, password, userId = null). Handler passes an account id when one is available; null until a source [39m
     [38;5;246mexists. Matches your request, existing call keeps working.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Client-generated tracking id
     [38;5;246mHandler generates a per-attempt id (crypto.randomUUID()) and passes it. Correlates log lines now, but identifies [39m
     [38;5;246mthe attempt rather than the person.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Server-assigned id in the result
     [38;5;246mKeep login's two params; carry the id on the returned object instead. Authoritative identity, but changes the [39m
